What:		/sys/class/net/<iface>/lin_ids/<id>
Date:		2026
KernelVersion:	6.18
Contact:	linux-can@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		For a LIN interface acting as a responder (client), each file
		<id> (hex, 00..3f) configures the answer published when the
		commander (host) sends a header with that identifier.

		Reading the file shows the stored answer:

			state cksum-mode is_event event_id n data cksum

		Writing configures it as a whitespace-separated list:

			<active> <cksum-mode> <is_event> <event_id> <n> <data...>

		where <active> and <is_event> are 0/1, <cksum-mode> is 0 for
		classic or 1 for enhanced, <event_id> and the <n> data bytes
		are hex, and <n> is the data length. An active answer carries
			1..8 bytes, a backend may reject <n> of 0.

		Only present on drivers that implement responder answers.
